WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.777
Next, every operation class gets a lane.

2
00:00:02.777 --> 00:00:05.240
This mapping is the program's inference.

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.118
Autonomous machine changes are SailPoint
lifecycle states and birthright access,

4
00:00:10.118 --> 00:00:13.279
but only for classes the
authorizing official listed.

5
00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:17.009
In ServiceNow, they're standard
changes, pre-authorized.

6
00:00:17.009 --> 00:00:20.879
Gated machine changes are approved
SailPoint access requests,

7
00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:25.843
or catalog items the spoke carries out, as
normal changes where the class needs one.

8
00:00:25.843 --> 00:00:30.535
Human decisions are certifications, or
a ServiceNow approval or change board.

9
00:00:30.535 --> 00:00:34.992
Certificates stay with the certificate
platform, outside both products.

10
00:00:34.992 --> 00:00:38.550
Disconnected applications
run as declared exceptions,

11
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.331
with a service desk ticket, a
recorded session and an end date.

12
00:00:42.331 --> 00:00:45.081
And emergencies go straight
to the change board.

13
00:00:45.081 --> 00:00:49.460
The authorizing official has to accept
any autonomous class in writing.
